Bound a wire string to the bytes that are there.

Deserialize<std::string> reads a 32-bit length off the wire and builds the
string from that many bytes without checking them against the end of the
datagram, so a peer announcement whose name claims a length of gigabytes
reads past the socket buffer. Every other deserializer in the file refuses a
short input with a range_error; this one now does the same.

Reachable by anyone on the network segment, through the Link Audio
messenger: a peer announcement carries the peer's name (PeerInfo) and its
channels' names (ChannelAnnouncements). The session discovery messages
carry no strings. Found by clockwork's Link wire fuzz target
(test/fuzz/fuzz_link_wire.cpp) in its first three minutes, 2026-10-28;
the input is corpus/link_wire/regressions/crash-0ae7e413.

One-file patch:
  - include/ableton/discovery/NetworkByteStreamSerializable.hpp

Wire protocol unchanged. A message that was previously an out-of-bounds
read is now refused as malformed, which every receiver already handles.

Pinned to Link-4.1.1.

diff --git a/include/ableton/discovery/NetworkByteStreamSerializable.hpp b/include/ableton/discovery/NetworkByteStreamSerializable.hpp
index 1ca8fdd..b67861c 100644
--- a/include/ableton/discovery/NetworkByteStreamSerializable.hpp
+++ b/include/ableton/discovery/NetworkByteStreamSerializable.hpp
@@ -335,7 +335,15 @@ struct Deserialize<std::string>
   {
     const auto result = Deserialize<uint32_t>::fromNetworkByteStream(
       std::move(bytesBegin), std::move(bytesEnd));
-    const auto endIt = std::next(result.second, result.first);
+    // CLOCKWORK PATCH: the length came off the wire; hold it to the bytes
+    // that are there, as every other deserializer here does, rather than
+    // reading past the datagram.
+    using ItDiff = typename std::iterator_traits<It>::difference_type;
+    if (std::distance(result.second, bytesEnd) < static_cast<ItDiff>(result.first))
+    {
+      throw std::range_error("String length exceeds the bytes available");
+    }
+    const auto endIt = std::next(result.second, static_cast<ItDiff>(result.first));
     return std::make_pair(std::string(result.second, endIt), endIt);
   }
 };
